## LangSmith adds behavior-based search over agent trajectories

Source: LangChain / LangSmith — https://www.langchain.com/blog/agent-traces-ai-search-langsmith
Published: 2026-10-13
Channel: news

LangSmith introduced AI Search for questions that cannot be reduced to a tag or an exact phrase. A decision model examines session trajectories against a natural-language description, such as an agent claiming completion without doing the work. SmithDB first narrows candidates with structured filters and normalizes repeated messages and tool activity into a common trajectory representation. The announcement describes a fixed context budget and acknowledges that evidence needed for some questions can be omitted. The feature is presented as a public beta, rather than a guarantee that every matching failure will be found.

For an operations team, this creates a useful way to discover examples for evaluation datasets and human review. Our editorial recommendation is to test searches against known positive and negative sessions, including failures visible only in tool results. Inspect missed matches as well as returned matches, and retain access to the complete trace when investigating a result. A fluent search explanation should not substitute for evidence that the requested action actually occurred.

Why it matters: Validate search recall against known failures before relying on it for incident discovery.

