## Assury proposes one audit and control layer across agent platforms

Source: Hacker News · David Girvi / Assury — https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50072334
Published: 2026-10-13
Channel: hn

Assury co-founder David Girvi announced cross-platform agent lifecycle management in a first-party Hacker News post. The founder describes automatic discovery and tagging across environments including AWS, Databricks, Snowflake, and Salesforce, with agent ownership visible in one place. The proposed control surface combines searchable audit records with kill and resume actions scoped by tags. The post also describes handling dynamically created agent swarms. These are vendor statements: this edition has not verified discovery completeness, record integrity, or the effectiveness of the incident controls.

The operational question is whether an inventory remains accurate when agents appear, change identity, or disappear during an investigation. Our editorial recommendation is to compare discovered agents with a small known inventory, exercise a tag-scoped stop in a test environment, and confirm that the resulting record identifies the caller, target, decision, and outcome. Keep execution telemetry distinct from inventory metadata. A centralized list of agents is useful, but it does not by itself establish why a particular tool action succeeded or failed.

Why it matters: Test inventory coverage and control outcomes before treating a central agent list as reliable evidence.

