Source: LangSmith · GitHub release — https://github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/releases/tag/v0.14.8
Published: 2026-10-13
Channel: github

LangSmith SDK v0.14.8 lists two Python changes directly affecting trace handling: sending session_id with RunTree.patch and making the fallback from a multipart upload endpoint returning 404 to the batch endpoint reachable. The release also contains sandbox-related changes and maintenance work. The notes identify the corrected paths but do not quantify how many users were affected, a loss-rate reduction, or a performance improvement. This edition focuses on the tracing changes rather than presenting the entire SDK release as an observability feature launch.

Our editorial recommendation is to validate both context continuity and delivery when updating a tracing SDK. Create a multi-turn canary that patches a run after its initial creation, then confirm that the resulting record belongs to the intended session. Where the deployment supports the documented fallback scenario, test an unavailable multipart endpoint and verify that the batch path preserves the expected records. Compare persisted data with the originating application events, including error cases. An SDK call completing without an exception is useful evidence, but it is not sufficient evidence that the backend stored the complete conversation correctly.

Why it matters: Verify persisted session associations and upload fallback behavior with an end-to-end canary.

