Source: OpenTelemetry · Dónal O’Sullivan — https://opentelemetry.io/blog/2026/hostmetrics-process-scraper-rc/
Published: 2026-10-13
Channel: news

OpenTelemetry describes versioned metric definitions for the hostmetrics process scraper in Collector Contrib v0.160.0. The mechanism keeps legacy and release-candidate definitions in the metadata schema, with feature gates controlling migration. Version suffixes are internal definition keys and are removed before emission. Some process metrics change names, units, or attributes; where definitions share an emitted name, migration must avoid publishing incompatible duplicates. The article invites users to test the release-candidate output and report broken dashboards before a later stability transition.

For AI workloads, process metrics remain useful context around model-serving workers, application runtimes, and telemetry collectors, even though this announcement is not an AI-specific instrument. Our editorial recommendation is to replay representative queries and alerts against the candidate schema, especially filters depending on renamed attributes. Compare sample records rather than checking only that a metrics endpoint responds. Keep a documented rollback path during the trial and annotate schema changes on operational dashboards. Otherwise an instrumentation upgrade can look like a workload improvement when a query has simply stopped selecting the intended series.

Why it matters: Validate query and alert semantics during schema migration, not just successful metric export.

